cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Extremal Selection as an Operational Substitute for Coexponentials: Fisher-Controlled Factorization"
message: "If you use this software or its formal results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Koch"
    given-names: "Brisen"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bbis-ops/Hypersurface-Categorical-Polytope"
url: "https://github.com/bbis-ops/Hypersurface-Categorical-Polytope"
abstract: >-
  Software and formal results for Fisher-controlled extremal probes and
  coproduct factorization on a bounded box, including the V.1-V.14 series on
  vertex localization: the interaction-strength threshold is exactly zero, with
  exact displacement and objective-gap laws, a directional law for coupled
  perturbations, an amplitude ceiling for saturating ridges, and a weighted
  anisotropic master law for the gap exponent. Model-proposed candidates are
  treated as untrusted data and adjudicated locally.
keywords:
  - coexponential
  - Fisher information
  - vertex localization
  - category theory
  - optimization
